<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Carbon Circle Holding AS, a subsidiary of GTH, signed frame agreement with Ocean GeoLoop AS on EPC services</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-12-23 09:59:08</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>OSLO – Dec 23,2022 – Carbon Circle Holding AS (CCH) and Ocean GeoLoop AS (OGL) has entered into a non-exclusive frame agreement for delivery of engineering, procurement and construction (EPC) services, related to OGL’s propriety carbon capture technology.<br><br>Both Odd-Geir Lademo, the CEO of OGL and CEO Aslak Hjelde of CCH express the importance of this agreement for the two companies.<br><br>“Ocean GeoLoop is one of the most exiting companies within the carbon capture space. It´s a great honour to support OGL and to reduce their clients carbon footprint,” says Hjelde.<br><br>OGL’s technology is currently being piloted at Norske Skog’s factory in Skogn – Trøndelag. The company’s end of pipe solution is easily integrated with the customer, connecting directly into the flue gas stack. This low complexity provides large savings compared to other carbon capture solutions. The robust process is designed to handle all flue gasses with minimal needs for special adoptions.<br><br>“The personell at Carbon Circle has solid EPC experience and track record. This cooporation will further leverage our capacity to develop and implement our carbon capture solution across interesting industrial segments in the years ahead,” says Lademo.<br><br>Carbon Circle delivers EPC projects from early phase studies to project execution and commissioning services. Building on over 30 years of experience from EPC contracts across a broad range of energy segments, from Oil & Gas to Energy-from-waste, Carbon Circle brings the necessary expertise to execute projects that help customers meet their ESG targets and partake in the energy transition.<br><br><br>For more information, please contact:<br>Aslak Hjelde, CEO Carbon Circle<br>Email: aslak@carboncircle.com<br>Phone: +47 908 50 969<br><br>About Carbon Circle<br>Carbon Circle offers an end-to-end solution, helping companies to fully integrate their operations into the CCS value chain. The company supports clients across a broad range of industries to develop their Carbon Capture & Storage (CCS) projects. We offer end-to-end carbon capture solutions, from initial analysis and feasibility studies to installation of a capture plant and transportation to permanent storage. By taking on the role of aggregating multiple sources of captured carbon we enable viable business cases and effective value chains.<br><br>For more information visit: www.carboncircle.com<br><br>About Ocean GeoLoop<br>Ocean GeoLoop is a green tech company aiming at using nature’s own way of solving the challenges of our time in a circular way. In 2022, the company introduces the GeoLoop CC technology that captures point source CO2 emissions, using natural and harmless processes, transforming the CO2 to a stable, liquid state. Ocean GeoLoop call this process “Carbon capture by nature.” The GeoLoop CC will help companies and countries around the globe to reach their goals of reduced emissions before 2030 and net zero by 2050. The company is listed on Oslo Børs Euronext Growth under the ticker OCEAN.<br><br>For more information visit: www.oceangeoloop.com</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
