<td><h2>News; Strengthening the GTH Team</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-11-25 14:58:58</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Green Transition Holding (ticker code: GTH) announce the following new appointments;<br>GTH are expanding group management with three new directors. This is an important step for the company as we are entering into the next phase of growth, developing and commercializing innovative technologies that improve the sustainability of industries.<br><br>Geir Otto Amundsen, Director<br>Mr. Amundsen started his position in August this year and holds significant international experience with more than 30 years’ experience working in various sectors, including general industry, oil and gas, aerospace, defense and renewables (offshore wind) and has worked with a range of businesses, including private, private equity and globally listed. He has held a range of directorships, including VP of Business Development, Head of Global Operations and CEO.<br>“I find GTH an exciting company with strong ownership and ambitious growth strategy. I look forward to contributing with my industrial experience and competence”, says Geir Otto.<br><br>Mikkel Andreasen, Chief of Staff<br>Mr. Andreasen started his position in October 2021. He has 5 years of corporate finance experience focusing primarily on the renewable energy and clean tech space. Prior to joining GTH, he worked in DNB Markets’ Investment Banking Division in Oslo and New York advising on a range of capital markets and M&A transactions. <br>“GTH is uniquely positioned to tackle the global waste problem and offer clean technology to replace fossil fuels. I am very excited to be a part of a highly ambitious team with strong industry know-how and commercial capabilities.” says Mikkel<br><br>Andreas Grav Karlsen, VP Business Development<br>Mr. Karlsen started his position in October and has 8 years of international experience in the oil and gas industry where he mainly focused on rig new builds and upgrades as well as offshore wind projects. He held various positions within engineering, new product development and sales. He has also held a central role in commercialization and development of low carbon solutions towards the oil and gas industry and project execution.<br>“GTH is a company that invests and focuses on technology and industries supporting the global energy transition. With a great team and big ambitions I look forward to being part of the growth of GTH ”, says Andreas.<br><br>“We are very pleased to bring Geir Otto, Mikkel and Andreas on board as we enter into the next growth phase of GTH. As we look forward, we expect there to be several growth opportunities for GTH. With our team’s experience GTH has the capabilities to develop and commercialize innovative technologies, improve efficiency, and minimize environmental footprints. This is always our main objective, and we expect this to also create shareholder value”, says Paal Skoe, CEO of GTH.<br><br>About GTH<br>Green Transition Holding (GTH) is an industrial and environmental technology company. Our mission is to develop and commercialize innovative technologies that improve the sustainability of industries. We aim to do this through reducing emissions, improve efficiency, and minimize the environmental footprint of these operations.<br>GTH was listed on the NOTC list in December 2020 and holds the ticker code GTH.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>GTH: Robert Hvide Macleod to join the Green Transition Holding Board of Directors</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-06-30 10:51:57</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Green Transition Holding (ticker code: GTH) announces that Robert Hvide Macleod will join its Board of Directors. Following the appointment, the Board will comprise of Eirik Flatebø (Chairman), Dag Schjerven (Director), Svein Flåtten (Director), Christopher Vanay (Director), Sigbjørn Bråtane (Director) and Robert Hvide Macleod (Director). In aggregate, the board holds approximately 1.5 million shares, representing approximately 12% of the shares outstanding. <br> <br>Mr Macleod holds significant international experience, and we expect that his expertise will prove valuable in the growth and development of GTH. He worked for AP Møller Maersk 2001-2004, Glencore International 2004-2011 and he served as the CEO of Frontline Management in the period 2014-2020. He now runs a portfolio of private equity investments and a number of them are in the renewables sector. GTH has recently been added to the portfolio and he currently controls 1% of the outstanding shares. <br> <br>"I view GTH as an exciting company, with a very solid customer base, and the team at GTH is highly skilled. Through its technology GTH is well positioned to continue to build its portfolio and I believe they will succeed in achieving rapid further growth. I look forward to working with the management and Board at what certainly is a very interesting time for the company", says Robert Hvide Macleod, new Board Member of GTH.<br> <br>"We are very pleased to bring Robert on to the GTH Board as we enter into next growth phase of GTH. As we look forward, we expect there to be a number of growth opportunities for GTH. We are able to develop and commercialize innovative technologies, improve efficiency, and minimize environmental footprints. This is always our main objective, and we expect this to also create shareholder value", says Eirik Flatebø, Chairman of GTH. <br> <br>About GTH<br>Green Transition Holding (GTH) is an industrial and environmental technology company. Our mission is to develop and commercialize innovative technologies that improve the sustainability of industries. We aim to do this through reducing emissions, improve efficiency, and minimize the environmental footprint of these operations. <br>GTH was listed on the NOTC list in December 2020 and holds the ticker code GTH.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>GTH: Green Transition Holding enters into partnership with Partner Energy and acquires a District Heating Portfolio</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-06-15 11:43:11</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Partner Energy (PE), an investment company with focus on Renewable Energy and Technology, and Green Transition Holding (GTH) an Industrial, Environmental Technology company, have entered into a partnership to own, develop and consolidate assets within the bioenergy segment. Combining, PE’s competence and group investments with GTH’s inhouse EPC, Otechos Services in a close Partnership, boosts competitiveness and provides a unique/[unparalleled] service catalogue to the bioenergy industry. “A partnership with PE strengthens GTH’s service levels and is essential to execute on GTH’s strategy to be a core provider of bioenergy in Norway”, says Paal Skoe, CEO of GTH. <br> <br>“Leveraging the strength for our Partnership, PE and GTH have already jointly acquired a portfolio of district heating bioenergy assets. These assets form the first fundament for further growth for the Partners within the green energy transition and an important step towards building a robust green energy portfolio to meet tomorrows customer’s demand for environmentally friendly energy generation solutions” the two CEO’s say.<br> <br>About Partner Energy<br>Partner Energy(PE) is a forward-thinking business partner and investor that builds, develops, and improves companies within renewable energy and technology. PE has extensive experience from the establishment, development and acquisition / sale of companies. Partnership as a collaboration tool is essential to ensure growth in the companies and positive development for customers, employees, management, and owners. “Focus on the green transition combined with active and value-creating owner a partnership with GTH brings an important value creating for our partners and future customers says Frank Håland, CEO of Partner Energy”…<br> <br>About GTH<br>Green Transition Holding (GTH) is an Industrial, Environmental Technology company developing and commercializing innovative technologies that improve the sustainability of industries by reducing emissions, improving efficiency, and minimizing the environmental footprint of these operations. GTH is listen on the NOTC-list in December 2020 with ticker code GTH.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>GTH and KANFA Group in advanced discussions about Partnership</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-06-09 15:03:10</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>KANFA Group and GTH in advanced discussions about partnership <br>KANFA Group, a global independent process house and offshore project execution specialist within the Oil & Gas Industry, and Green Transition Holding (GTH) an Industrial, Environmental Technology company, are in discussions to jointly Engineer, Procure and Construct (EPC) Waste to Energy (WTE) plants globally. The partnership brings GTH one step closer to provide high efficiency small to mid-scale turn-key WTE plants to the waste incineration industry. “Together with GTH’s inhouse EPC, Otechos Services and the partnership with AITOS gasification waste incineration technology, KANFA Group’s competence is essential to execute GTH’s strategy to build, own and operate waste incineration plants globally “says Paal Skoe, CEO of GTH. <br> <br>About KANFA Group<br>KANFA Group is an independent process house and project execution specialist within the Energy Industry. KANFA Group delivers complete topside process EPC contracts, modules, packages, equipment, FEED studies and services such as troubleshooting and revamp as well as optimisation studies. «The KANFA way» combines extensive market knowledge with multi-discipline experience to provide superior process designs and technical solutions to our clients’ best advantage – monetary engineering. The focus is on cost, project execution, performance and quality. “A partnership with GTH is a clear strategy for KANFA to utilize the «The KANFA way» in an exciting market with clear synergies with our experience and competence within the Group” says Aslak Hjelde, CEO of KANFA Group<br> <br>The KANFA Group is a fully owned subsidiary of Technip Energies.<br> <br>About GTH<br>Green Transition Holding (GTH) is an Industrial, Environmental Technology company developing and commercializing innovative technologies that improve the sustainability of industries by reducing emissions, improving efficiency, and minimizing the environmental footprint of these operations. GTH is listed on the NOTC-list with ticker code GTH and ISIN NO0010905029.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Rettet emisjon / Private Placement in Green Transition Holding AS</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-03-08 12:51:45</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Rettet emisjon i Green Transition Holding AS<br><br>Styret i Green Transition Holding AS mottok i midten av februar 2021 en henvendelse fra en gruppe interessante investorer som ønsket å investere i selskapet.<br><br>Ut i fra dette, besluttet styret å gjennomføre en rettet emisjon på til sammen 517.800 aksjer på kurs NOK 25,- per aksje. Transaksjonen er gjennomført og lukket.<br><br><br>Private placement in Green Transition Holding AS<br><br>During February 2021, the board of directors of Green Transition Holding AS has been approached by a group of interesting investors intending to invest in the company.<br><br>Against this background, the board resolved to issue 517.800 new shares, each NOK 25,- per share in a directed private placement. The transaction has been completed and is now closed. <br><br>Date / place<br>08.03.2021 / Akland, Norway</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>GTH: Green Transition Holding AS is registered on the NOTC-list</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-03-01 11:29:47</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Green Transition Holding AS is registered on the NOTC-list as of 21 December 2020 with ticker code GTH. The company has issued 12,237,027 shares each with a par value NOK 0.01, all of which is registered in the VPS with ISIN code NO 001 0905029. Based on the last traded price (equity issue closed on 30 September 2020) the market capitalization is NOK 174,989,486.10 (NOK 14.30 per share). The company has entered into an agreement whereby it will be able to use the NOTC reporting system as from 21 December 2020.<br><br>Green Transition Holding (GTH) is an Industrial, Environmental Technology company developing and commercializing innovative technologies that improve the sustainability of industries by reducing emissions, improving efficiency, and minimizing the environmental footprint of these operations.<br><br>With the AITOS gasification waste incineration technology, GTH will contribute significantly to improve efficiency and reduce emissions from existing waste-to-energy (WTE) plants. Together with our inhouse EPC, OTECHOS Services, GTH will present a new generation low emission, high efficiency small to mid-scale WTE plant solution to the waste incineration industry. Building, owning and operating modern, efficient WTE units is part of GTE’s long-term strategy.<br>With the PIPEOTECH DVS sealing technology, GTH has introduced the world’s first fully certified, 100% gastight flange seal setting new environmental standards by curbing fugitive emissions and improving HSE standards in numerous industries such as plastic recycling, district heating, shipping, chemistry and petrochemicals. Having built a solid base of initial commercial customers and a highly experienced team, PIPEOTECH is entering a phase of rapidly expanding global sales.<br>GTH represents a unique combination of proven and new technologies, industrial capabilities, experienced resources, and established revenue streams from operating units. PIPEOTECH AS and OTECHOS Services AS are 100% daughter companies of GTH. GTH holds a 10% stake in Aitos Gasification Technology AS and an option to acquire the remaining shares of the company on certain terms.<br><br>Please see attached Company Presentation.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
